<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
    Retires exactly ONE permission set: Transaction_App_Access

    Each stage under manifest/permset-retirement/ is independent and separately runnable, so a
    soak or a rollback on one set never blocks another.

    DELETION IS IRREVERSIBLE IN THE ORG. Do not run this until every step for this set in
    docs/permission-set-retirement-runbook.md is complete: the residual closed and deployed, the
    replacement sets ASSIGNED IN-ORG, the in-org VERIFY signed off, and this set unassigned from
    every user and removed from every permission set group.

    A set that is still assigned, or that is still a permission set group member, makes this
    deploy FAIL, and it fails AFTER any constructive half of the same deploy has already applied.

    The exact deploy command is in the runbook, section 5. It is deliberately NOT reproduced here
    because an XML comment cannot contain a double hyphen, which every sf CLI flag begins with.
    -->
    <types>
        <members>Transaction_App_Access</members>
        <name>PermissionSet</name>
    </types>
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
